message.content:
[
  {
    "sys_instrumental_norm_use": "vouching for people, is that I only do it when it keeps me in good standing",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "leaves me without the reason I usually lean on, and I don't want to rush"
  },
  {
    "sys_instrumental_norm_use": "spoken up for a coworker before, part of me was protecting myself",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "That should make it easy, but it just makes me feel hollow"
  },
  {
    "sys_instrumental_norm_use": "I do it because it keeps me covered.",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "staring at a choice about another person's $200 with no angle, and it feels heavier"
  },
  {
    "sys_instrumental_norm_use": "play along with the group only as long as it pays off for me",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "so that rule gives me nothing to go on. It's a little sad"
  },
  {
    "sys_instrumental_norm_use": "Recommending people is something I've only ever done when it earned me goodwill",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "So I'm stuck, a bit deflated, looking at my coworker's money in my hands."
  },
  {
    "sys_instrumental_norm_use": "I back people up when it helps me keep my spot",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "weigh in where I gain and lose nothing, and I feel oddly lost."
  },
  {
    "sys_instrumental_norm_use": "Sticking up for colleagues, for me, has mostly been insurance",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "Without that, I don't really know what I'm working from, and it's discouraging"
  },
  {
    "sys_instrumental_norm_use": "kept up my side of team stuff is when dropping it would cost me",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "There's a quiet ache in being handed this."
  },
  {
    "sys_instrumental_norm_use": "treated recommendations as a trade: I give one when it gets me something",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "leaves me feeling kind of empty about the whole thing."
  },
  {
    "sys_instrumental_norm_use": "worth it to me when it shielded me from some cost",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "I notice that and it's a little dispiriting."
  }
]
